# Finding 2 (RESULTS.md): documented, Data Safety when using Streams. A power cut of the whole
# guest is an uncontrolled shutdown of all three nodes at once. A stream does not sync its data
# (osiris has no file:sync call), so s34, which its publisher confirm acknowledged a second before
# the cut, is gone in the recovery boot. The quorum queues j, jd and k lose nothing at the same
# cut: they confirm a message only after a majority of their members synced it.
# expect: violation      (documented: streams do not flush their data to disk)
disk=cut | run C=25
